  },
  {
   "id": "p86-out-e10",
   "page": 86,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Medication side-effect likely • Discuss with doctor whether to stop or change medication. Continue medication only if necessary. • Advise to return if rash develops or itch persists.",
   "bbox": [
    281.2,
    272.8,
    474.0,
    313.8
   ],
   "key": "p86-705cb0c3"
  },
  {
   "id": "p86-out-e11",
   "page": 86,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• If severe itch, give chlorphenamine 4mg at night, or 6-8 hourly for up to 5 days. Can cause sedation. • If long-term itch, give instead cetirizine 10mg daily.",
   "bbox": [
    320.6,
    409.6,
    701.7,
    430.4
   ],
   "key": "p86-c9e2aa15"
  },
  {
   "id": "p86-out-e12",
   "page": 86,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Did the patient start any new medication in the weeks before the itch started?",
   "bbox": [
    392.9,
    225.5,
    679.3,
    235.7
   ],
   "key": "p86-49892321"
  },
  {
   "id": "p86-out-e13",
   "page": 86,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• If itch persists > 2 weeks: - Test for anaemia 44, HIV 124 and diabetes 19. - Refer to doctor same day.",
   "bbox": [
    528.2,
    366.2,
    735.1,
    396.4
   ],
   "key": "p86-ceb136ec"
  },
  {
   "id": "p86-out-e14",
   "page": 86,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• Advise to: - Avoid hot baths, wool/itchy fabrics and scratching as these may worsen itch. - Wash with aqueous cream (UEA) instead of soap. Avoid using aqueous cream as moisturiser. - Moisturise skin with emulsifying ointment (UE) twice a day. - Avoid scrubbing the skin and washing more than once a day. Gently pat skin dry. - Keep nails short and clean. • If known with a life-limiting illness, also give palliative care 191.",
   "bbox": [
    218.8,
    444.3,
    574.9,
    514.5
   ],
   "key": "p86-71db33f1"
  },
  {
   "id": "p86-out-e15",
   "page": 86,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "If no better or diagnosis uncertain, discuss/refer.",
